      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters instead of dropping them: `café` gives `cafe`, and `Crème Brûlée` gives `creme-brulee`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass, including a new one for the accented cases.\n\nThe fix is in `slug/core.py`. Accented letters are decomposed with NFKD and reduced to their ASCII base. A small map handles letters that don't decompose: `ß`→`ss`, `æ`→`ae`, `œ`→`oe`, `ø`→`o`, `ł`→`l`, `đ`/`ð`→`d`, `þ`→`th`.\n\nLetters with no ASCII equivalent (for example Greek or Cyrillic) are still dropped, as before. Turning them into dashes or romanizing them would be a separate decision, so I left that alone.\n\nI also added `test_accented_letters_are_transliterated` to `tests/test_core.py`, which you didn't ask for. It's three assertions and easy to remove if you don't want it.",
